(D/'README.md').write_text('''# Airstrike Console obstruction repair (source/test only)

The retained800x600 startup image shows Console over Airstrike and the visible prompt “Press any key to start”. Original production Controller.run refuses that exact observation with zero commands. It remains a valid refusal unless a reviewer explicitly authorizes the narrow startup action.

The repair uses ordinary activation through the exposed Airstrike titlebar. The pinned runner accepts click:x:y, queues it at the frozen boundary, and drains it through renderer.handleMouseDown/Up. The pinned renderer raises the titlebar target and transfers keyboard ownership/focus through its normal input path. At the retained geometry the safe point is656,33, to the right of Console and clear of Airstrike caption buttons. The earlier considered minimize route was discarded because clicking Console transfers focus to Console.

A reviewer must bind session/token/sha256/after to the actual capture and supply consoleObstruction equal to the full Console window record, startupPrompt “Press any key to start”, keysReleased true, unobscured false and evidence equal to the request capture path. The bridge supplies startupSnapshot from its own pinned capture, never trusting reviewer-supplied state. Only the exact two-window Airstrike1.0pre6/Console identity and a safe exposed caption point are accepted. Any changed image, focus, whole snapshot, stale lease or wrong click stops before dispatch. There is no blind Console close or process action.

Activation completion requires real input log plus a full one-batch ACK and frozen-zero snapshot. A new reviewed unobscured startup image with Airstrike focus is required before Space32; a new gameplay/menu observation follows release. The existing observed-row navigation and strict guest-exit normal-Quit validation are preserved. No menu, gameplay or ordinary Quit was accepted in this offline task.

Run test/test-airstrike-console-obscuration.py with Python-B under the assigned lightweight pool/trusted supervisor. Its actual controller CLI and Bridge.run fixtures are explicitly fake transport, not guest execution. receipt.json binds source/production hashes and evidence. evidence/reused-baseline.json reuses historical25 total regressions including12 bridge cases without claiming historical hashes qualify changed source. The new focused10 tests cover the changed behavior; the original controller fails the new transition oracle as expected. Source-review diff and unchanged terminal/ACK/cleanup AST checks are retained.

This is a sparse orphan report branch. Integrate only the two changed tools and the new test after independent acceptance; do not merge this whole tree. Evidence files and immutable external donor references are recovery material. Main and all runtime lifecycle operations remain coordinator/assigned-owner controlled. See receipt.json for the next runtime gates. No Node/API/Boat/guest execution or public deployment occurred.
''')
